{
  "reason": "The 0.7448 baseline is limited because neither base learner receives an explicit coupon×context acceptance prior: DeepFM only embeds coupon/gender/maritalStatus/occupation, and HistGBM must approximate 125-level coupon×occupation interactions via axis-aligned one-hot splits. The initial plan's leakage-safe smoothed target encoding is the highest-leverage, lowest-risk change because historical experiments on this exact UCI task show that ordered/leakage-safe target statistics for coupon-context cells gave the single most reliable lift (CatBoost's ordered target statistics), and the successful merged pipeline already proved per-fold stateful FeatureEngineer fitting plus artifact persistence works. These changes belong in data_processing_and_feature_engineering (new encoded features and their fitted mappings) and training_evaluation (fold-safe fitting, inner-K-fold for the final refit, and persistence/load of encoders), while base model architectures and the blend/threshold search remain unchanged to preserve the working contract.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Extend FeatureEngineer with leakage-safe smoothed target encoders (Bayesian smoothing toward the training prior, strength ~20-30) for seven coupon-context keys: coupon, occupation, coupon×occupation, coupon×time, coupon×expiration, coupon×distance_bucket, coupon×direction_same. Emit each as a dense float column (smoothed posterior, plus optional logit variant) named e.g. te__coupon, te__coupon_x_occupation; keep all existing ordinal, frequency, one-hot, missingness, habit_match, and interaction features byte-for-byte unchanged and appended after the current columns so feature_columns ordering stays deterministic and the reindex in transform() still guarantees alignment. WHY: trees cannot cheaply express the 125-cell coupon×occupation interaction from one-hots, and DeepFM never sees it as a field; smoothed group priors condense that signal into one robust dense feature and borrow strength for rare/missing combinations (occupation has 25 levels), controlling variance. HOW: Add FeatureEngineer attributes self.te_prior (global mean), self.te_maps (key -> {level: (smoothed_value, count)}) and self.te_smoothing; build keys in fit() from already-computed numeric columns (time_num, expiration_num, distance_bucket, direction_same_num, occupation/coupon strings) so no new raw parsing is introduced; transform() applies maps with prior fallback for unseen levels and missing keys and writes 0.5 default only when prior is absent. INTERFACE: widen fit(self, df, y=None) with y optional so existing FeatureEngineer().fit(df) calls still work; transform(df) signature and returned DataFrame dtype float32 and feature_columns reindex behavior are unchanged; all learned state must live on the FE instance so pickling fe in meta.pkl transfers encoders to the fresh predict process without refitting.",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Make target-encoding fit strictly fold-safe and persist it as part of the existing artifacts. In run_oof, call FeatureEngineer().fit(features_df.iloc[tr], y=y_int[tr]) so every outer fold's encoder (and its smoothing prior) is estimated only on the outer-train rows and merely applied to the outer-validation rows via transform(); in final_fit, generate the training-row encoded values with an inner StratifiedKFold (5 folds, shuffle=True, random_state=42) so no row ever sees its own label, then fit a final FeatureEngineer on all training rows with y=y_int for prediction-time transform. WHY: the initial plan requires that validation scores stay honest and that the final model not leak its own targets; the historical successful merged pipeline already fits stateful preprocessing per fold and reloads it read-only in a new process, so extending that proven pattern to the new encoder is the safe route, and it composes with the existing blend-weight/threshold search without changing architectures. HOW: add a small helper (e.g. build_inner_kfold_te(features_df, y_int) -> DataFrame view with OOF-encoded training rows) invoked only for the final fit; keep the existing 5-fold StratifiedKFold(random_state=42) assignment, per-fold scaler stats, GBM construction, DeepFM bagging seeds (42 + fi*10 + b), blend grid search, and final refit flow untouched; ensure the saved meta.pkl already pickles the FE instance so te_prior/te_maps ship with it, and predict_pipeline continues to use fe.transform(features) only, never fit. INTERFACE: preserve run_oof / final_fit / save_artifacts / load_artifacts / predict_pipeline signatures and the row_id/prediction output contract; only the FE.fit call sites gain the y argument and an OOF-encoding helper is added; log the chosen smoothing strength and the OOF encoded-feature StratifiedKFold seed in the training stdout for reproducibility under the 600s/2-thread budget."
  }
}
